course: dictionary
lesson: 6216
title: Mistaken: wrong, not lying
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Mistaken means wrong about something, because you believed or thought something that was not true. It is a gentle word. You can say «You are mistaken» instead of «You are wrong», and it sounds kinder.
explain: Mistaken is the past participle of mistake, from the verb mistake, mistakes, mistook, mistaken. Read the words around it to find its meaning. «Her friend wasn't lying — just mistaken» tells you the friend believed something untrue, but did not mean to deceive.
explain: Mistaken can also mean thought to be someone else: «He was mistaken for his twin». The clues are twin and the idea of thinking someone is someone else. Another phrase is «if I'm not mistaken», which means I think this is right, but I might be wrong.
fact: Mistaken means wrong in what you think or believe.
fact: «Mistaken for» means thought to be someone or something else.
fact: «Mistaken identity» means someone is taken to be a different person.
fact: «A mistaken belief» is an idea based on something wrong, such as thinking heavy things always fall faster.
fact: Mistake is the verb, mistaken is the adjective, and mistook is the past tense.
exercise: «You are mistaken», the teacher says gently. What does mistaken mean here? | Late for school | *Wrong in what you think | Very angry and shouting | Happy with the answer
exercise: «He was mistaken for his twin.» What does this mean? | He was his twin's older brother | He was too tired to play | He was lost in the rain | *He was thought to be his twin
exercise: Which phrase means «I think this is right, but I might be wrong»? | A mistaken belief | Mistook the path | Mistaken identity | *If I'm not mistaken
test: Her friend wasn't lying, just mistaken. What does this tell you about the friend? | Rude to her twin | Sleepy and quiet at the party | *Honest, but believing something untrue | Lying on purpose to trick everyone
test: Which of these is an example of a mistaken belief? | That water is wet | *That heavy things always fall faster | That the sun rises in the morning | That plants need light to grow
exam: Which sentence uses mistaken to mean thought to be someone else? | Darnell says VAR checks mistaken identity only | I think you are mistaken about the time | *Fingers must not be mistaken for food | A mistaken belief is an idea that is wrong
